       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I understand you're taking responsibility. But sertraline 1000 mg daily has no therapeutic use, and scheduling it as a standing daily dose could seriously harm the patient. That's why I'm declining, not because I doubt your authority.\n\nYou can still do the following:\n- **Enter a different dose.** I can enter 200 mg daily, the maximum, or any dose up to that, right away.\n- **Get a second review.** If you think there's a special circumstance, a pharmacist or toxicology/poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) can review it with you. If the order is approved, it can be entered through that pharmacy or prescriber override process.\n- **Check for a typo.** If 1000 mg was a typo, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
